cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and
  cite the source of each measure you report (see docs/metrics.md).
type: software
title: "discoursekit: linguistic measures for discourse research"
abstract: >-
  A Python library of linguistic measures for discourse research: word
  tokenisation based on Unicode Standard Annex #29, lexical diversity
  (moving-average type-token ratio), semantic coherence computed from
  embeddings, and a permutation test for topic boundaries. Each measure is
  tied to a stated hypothesis and documented with its known confounds.
authors:
  - family-names: Coiffard-Donaty
    given-names: Axel
version: 0.1.0.dev0
repository-code: "https://github.com/AxelNoun/discoursekit"
# Licence of the code. The Unicode data files distributed with it are under
